# Production frontend/.env for mroueali.com.
#
# Copy to /home/ali/apps/Portfolio/frontend/.env on the server. Vite reads this
# at BUILD time and inlines the values into the bundle — so it is baked in by
# deploy.sh, and changing it means rebuilding, not restarting. Nothing secret
# belongs in here: every VITE_ variable ships to the browser in plain text.

# VITE_API_URL is deliberately left unset.
#
# Unset, the app requests /api/... on its own origin, which nginx proxies to the
# backend on 127.0.0.1:8000. One origin means no CORS preflight, no mixed-content
# risk, and no second certificate. Set it only if the API ever moves to its own
# subdomain — and then add that origin to CORS_ORIGINS in backend/.env.
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.mroueali.com

# Points the ask bar at the real backend instead of the answers bundled at build
# time. Relative on purpose — same origin, so it inherits the site's scheme and
# host, and /api/ask/stream (which the code derives by appending /stream) gets
# the SSE proxy settings from the nginx block.
VITE_ASK_API=/api/ask

# Dev-only; the production build never starts a dev server, so it is unused here.
# VITE_API_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:8000
